{
  "comment": "The vectors pinning Prima.Confirmation: every side reads each record, writes it back to the same map and reproduces its digest, sha256:<hex> over the JCS bytes of the whole record with the protocol string, home, rp_id and preview included, and a record changed in any one field digests differently; and refuses each refusal with the named reason. A preview is secret-free: a detail named as a secret is refused. The rp_id is the home's host or a parent domain of it. A record is named by its ref, never by the secret id its signal answered: the ref is cnr_ followed by the unpadded base64url SHA-256 of the ref protocol string followed by the id, and every side derives the vector's ref from its id.",
